From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:36:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: samsung: exynos-pmu: add google,gs201-pmu

gs201 (Tensor G2) has gs101's PMU: the same secure register access
through the EL3 monitor, the same CPU hotplug and reboot-mode controls
and the same PMU interrupt generator, so exynos-pmu uses gs101's data
for it. Document it with google,gs101-pmu as the fallback, so the
gs101 rules (no syscon, the required interrupt generator phandle, the
reboot modes) apply.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
index d594982f2..7aedd2e7c 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
@@ -15,6 +15,9 @@ properties:
       - enum:
           - google,gs101-pmu
           - google,zuma-pmu
+      - items:
+          - const: google,gs201-pmu
+          - const: google,gs101-pmu
       - items:
           - const: google,zumapro-pmu
           - const: google,zuma-pmu
